  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya Refugee Operations Funding 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KRCS plays a critical role in delivering humanitarian services to refugees and host communities in the Kakuma&#x2013;Kalobeyei and Dadaab complexes, which together accommodate over 735,000 refugees and asylum seekers&#x2014;far beyond their intended capacities. Following funding cuts from USAID and reduced funding from UNHCR, the humanitarian situation in these refugee camps has severely deteriorated.&#xa0;This has resulted in the scaling down or suspension of essential health, nutrition, and protection services, increasing risks to life and dignity among refugees and host communities.&#xa0;This the humanitarian situation is made worse by ongoing epidemics outbreaks in refugee camps including a current active Cholera situation.
Kenya Red Cross is seeking support from BRC to help bridge the funding gap towards the refugee operations to sustain the running of the camps and hospitals that serve both refugees and host communities living within Dadaab and Kakuma.</narrative>
  </description>
